From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reilly Brogan <reilly@reillybrogan.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] tests: resolve netgroups from files

aerynOS's default nsswitch.conf uses "netgroup: nis" (glibc's historical
default). The test harness replaces /etc with test/data/etc, which ships no
nsswitch.conf, so netgroup lookups fall back to the nis provider and never
match, making rules_netgroup_membership_with_member fail.

Ship a minimal nsswitch.conf in the test data that resolves netgroups from
files; every other database keeps glibc's built-in default.

Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-15
---
 test/data/etc/nsswitch.conf | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)
 create mode 100644 test/data/etc/nsswitch.conf

diff --git a/test/data/etc/nsswitch.conf b/test/data/etc/nsswitch.conf
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..f74405169
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/data/etc/nsswitch.conf
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+netgroup: files
